# The Missing Prisoners

## Scene summary (from gm-assist, verbatim)

#### The party discovers that the prisoners they had left behind are gone, their chains torn apart and their bodies claimed by the necromancer.

- The party checks on the four prisoners it had left without food for several days, with the DM noting that no one knows whether they are still alive.
- Upon arrival, the captives are missing.
- Zephyr rolls a 22 on Investigation and discovers that the chains have been torn apart.
- The prisoners did not escape; their corpses have been taken and apparently added to the necromancer’s undead forces.
- The group concludes that its “friendly neighborhood necromancer” is becoming increasingly troublesome.
- The party discusses administrative roles, with Calmer designating Zephyr as Chief of Staff and Zinnia as Chief of Security.
- Calmer does not hold the titles steady — he later asks Zinnia to approve “my Chief of Operations plan.” The wobble is his, not the transcript’s: he is inventing the org chart as he goes and has not settled what he has appointed anyone to.
- Sequoia is reminded that he oversees supplies and summarizes his role as, “I’m in charge of getting shit done.”
- Zephyr proposes posting notices throughout the temple ordering anyone who finds information about the necromancer to report it.
- Calmer enthusiastically approves and tells Zephyr, “Produce an appropriate note, and I will sign it.”
- Calmer then questions whether hunting the necromancer should properly be Zinnia’s initiative as Chief of Security.
- Zinnia approves the plan, and the party decides to draft the notice after finishing its exploration.

## Verbatim moments

**GM** — *pointing out the prisoners the party abandoned*
> "So there's, like, this area… there's this dark area over here, and then there's these prisoners… let me just put them here…"

**GM** — *on their condition*
> "that you kind of left for the last few days, Lord knows if they're still alive."

**GM** — *locating the prisoners*
> "Over here."

**GM** — *checking that the party can see them*
> "Right, you should see some prisoners over there."

**Sequoia** — *confirming*
> "Totally."

**Zinnia** — *confirming*
> "Oh, yeah, I see them."

**GM** — *reiterating their abandonment*
> "Yeah, right. Okay, so there's these prisoners that you guys kind of left over there. Lord knows if they're still alive."

**Zephyr** — *realizing the problem*
> "Wait."

**Zephyr** — *on the prisoners’ lack of provisions*
> "Yeah, they have no food."

**GM** — *confirming*
> "Yep, they have no food, they've kind of been abandoned for a few days."

**Zephyr** — *suggesting a use for them*
> "Do we feed them to the Minotaur?"

**GM** — *checking what Zephyr proposed*
> "Do you feed them to the Minotaur? Is that… was that what you just said?"

**Sequoia** — *asking about the prisoners*
> "Are they dead?"

**GM** — *noting that the party has not checked yet*
> "Well, you haven't gone there, like, I'm just asking, that's…"

**Sequoia** — *considering what to do if they are dead*
> "Check it out, if they're dead, then we…"

**GM** — *revealing the empty prison*
> "You arrive there, and they are missing."

**GM** — *returning to the discovery*
> "Right, so you arrive there, and the minute…"

**GM** — *restating the discovery after an OOC interruption*
> "Anyway, alright, so you arrive there, and the, prisoners are missing."

**GM** — *calling for a check*
> "Roll an Investigation, Religion check, whatever you guys want."

**Zephyr** — *choosing his approach*
> "I'll investigate."

**GM** — *requesting the result*
> "Alright, tell me what you rolled."

**Zephyr** — *reporting his Investigation roll*
> "22?"

**GM** — *revealing what happened to the prisoners*
> "Alright. So, yes, in fact, they are missing, and as you look around, you realize that they didn't escape - they were killed, and their corpses have been taken."

**GM** — *pointing out the damaged restraints*
> "But that, you know, you notice how the chains have been torn apart."

**GM** — *connecting the stolen bodies to the necromancer*
> "You speculate that your friendly neighborhood necromancer has added them to the list of bodies he's controlling."

**Zephyr** — *reacting*
> "All good."

**GM** — *on the loss*
> "So… Very unfortunate."

**GM** — *on the escalating threat*
> "But, your friendly neighborhood necromancer is starting to, be more and more irritating."

**GM** — *asking what the party will do next*
> "Which way do you want to go?"

**Zephyr** — *considering pursuit*
> "tracking?"

**GM** — *reminding the party that it can delegate*
> "Well, I mean, you can track him, you can send… don't forget, you're the big bosses, you can send your troops to go track him."

**Zephyr** — *proposing a notice*
> "Alright, I'll… I'll post, like, I mean, I'll make…"

**Zephyr** — *assigning the notice to Calmer*
> "Calmer post, like, a notice saying, if you find this necromancer, you have to tell us."

**GM** — *as Calmer, approving the idea and assigning responsibility*
> "Calmer goes, I think that's a fantastic idea, Zephyr. As the Chief of Staff, I think you are responsible for all matters related to security operations. Produce an appropriate note, and I will sign it."

**Zephyr** — *accepting*
> "Correct."

**GM** — *as Calmer, reconsidering the chain of command*
> "But then he pauses. But I do feel, I turn to Zinnia, as my chief of security, shouldn't this really be your initiative?"

**Sequoia** — *questioning his place in the organization*
> "The heck of my job around here."

**GM** — *asking him to repeat himself*
> "What?"

**Sequoia** — *asking directly*
> "What is my job around here?"

**GM** — *trying to recall the appointment*
> "Your job… we established your job, didn't we?"

**Sequoia** — *denying it*
> "No."

**GM** — *insisting*
> "We… we didn't? Yeah, we did."

**GM** — *listing the posts*
> "Your job is, there's Chief of staff, Chief of Security."

**GM** — *describing Sequoia’s duty more bluntly*
> "Chief of making sure my shit doesn't get stolen."

**GM** — *settling on supplies*
> "You're in charge of, supplies."

**Sequoia** — *accepting*
> "Yep."

**GM** — *as Calmer, asking Zinnia to review the proposal under yet another title*
> "So, Zinnia?"

**GM** — *seeking approval*
> "Do you agree with my Chief of Operations plan, or do you think there's a more subtle way we could go about it?"

**Zinnia** — *asking to hear the plan again*
> "Can you repeat the plan, just to make sure?"

**GM** — *as Calmer, restating Zephyr’s proposal*
> "Well, well, according to Zephyr… Zephyr, if… correct me if I got it wrong."

**GM** — *describing the proposed notices*
> "He's proposing that we put out bills everywhere, announcing that we're looking for a necromancer, and that everyone, if anyone has any information, to come straight to us."

**Zephyr** — *confirming*
> "Yep."

**Zinnia** — *approving*
> "I think we should do that, yeah."

**GM** — *as Calmer, enthusiastically authorizing the plan*
> "You think we should do that? Excellent, excellent! I will then carry all the details, I… just bring me something to sign. Alright."

**GM** — *noting that they must return to draft it*
> "But, in the meantime, we're not… we probably need to go back if we want to do that."

**GM** — *offering the immediate choice*
> "Alright, so do you want to keep exploring or head back to your, offices? You've pretty much explored everything except these last two areas."

**Zinnia** — *favoring a return*
> "There you go back."

**Sequoia** — *favoring continued exploration*
> "Let's go, I'm a completionist, let's go explore those areas."
